## Summary

We will build a financial eligibility (means test) journey with [hmpps-forge](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/hmpps-forge). It will live in this repository as a single, self-contained module (`src/eligibility/`).

The module will have clear boundaries, so that:

- cla-operator-app can mount it under a case
- another service can copy the folder into its own codebase and mount it the same way
- it can later be published as a package without restructuring

The questions, their order and the branching rules come from **Check if your client qualifies for legal aid (CCQ)**. Business analysis (BA) and user-centred design (UCD) work established what an eligibility service needs to ask and in what order, and CCQ is the result. We are reusing that knowledge, not CCQ's Rails code.

