## Risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Sessions use express-session `MemoryStore` (`utils/session.ts`), which keeps each session in one pod's memory. Staging runs 2 replicas and production 4, with no session affinity (found in spike S3), so this already affects the app, not just this journey: a request sent to a different pod loses the session, including SiLAS sign-in. | Redis is being added in an open pull request (D8). On 6 October 2026 only `laa-cla-operator-app-uat` had an ElastiCache resource in `cloud-platform-environments`. Staging, training and production need one before the journey reaches them. |
| A second CFE call, and possibly a different result: today, every save through cla_backend's eligibility check API calls CFE and overwrites `state` and `calculations`. This includes saves that only change other fields, such as `category`. cla_backend builds a different payload from ours, and until production it calls a different CFE environment (D7). | A cla_backend change so this module's result is stored without a CFE call (D9, Q3). Until it ships, do not save eligibility answers through the existing endpoint. The operator app's `ResultHandler` builds `state` and `calculations` in cla_backend's shape, ported from `_translate_response`. This stays in the host, not the module, because the shape belongs to cla_backend. |
| Staging, training and UAT use CFE staging (D7), whose thresholds or behaviour may run ahead of production. | Before go-live, run the parity fixtures against CFE production. |
| Forge is pre-1.0 (0.4.x), so its API may change. | Pin the version. Keep Forge-specific code in `journey/` and `registries/` so `domain/` is unaffected. |
| Forge declares Node 20/22/24 support, but this app runs Node 26. | Confirm with the Forge maintainers, or test explicitly. |
| A second copy of Forge (`ts-app/node_modules`) could cause duplicate-instance bugs if bundled. | Remove the stray `ts-app/`. List Forge as a peer dependency if the module is extracted. |
| Parity drift: CCQ changes after the port. | Pin the CCQ commit the port is based on (currently `1a30ea3f`). Re-run parity fixtures when CCQ changes. |
| The create-case redirect bug (`search-client/step.ts:66` resolves to `/receive-call/cases/<ref>`) makes `/case/:caseId` unreachable. | Fix before mounting the eligibility journey under the case journey. |

